    "text": "1 days ago The Mentor Lagoons Nature Preserve and Marina holds a storied place in our community’s history. It was here, in 1797, that the first permanent settlement in the Western Reserve was established when Charles Parker, a member of Moses Cleaveland’s surveying team, built his cabin near the intersection of what is now Hopkins Road and Lake Shore Boulevard. Read full article",
